1wv9|a|Of or pertaining to romance; involving or resembling romance; hence, fanciful; marvelous; extravagant; unreal; as, a romantic tale; a romantic notion; a romantic undertaking. ; Entertaining ideas and expectations suited to a romance; as, a romantic person; a romantic mind. ; Of or pertaining to the style of the Christian and popular literature of the Middle Ages, as opposed to the classical antique; of the nature of, or appropriate to, that style; as, the romantic school of poets. ; Characterized by strangeness or variety; suggestive of adventure; suited to romance; wild; picturesque; -- applied to scenery; as, a romantic landscape.	j:19r7,119,3;1uxe,107,66;1ozy,103,4;1lkx,94,7;1uxd,89,67;1lku,88,13;tru,78,8;1uxc,78,4;1hke,71,4;15td,56,14;19vp,42,5;12m4,33,7~1uxd,89,67;1uxe,107,66;15td,56,14;1lku,88,13;tru,78,8;1lkx,94,7;12m4,33,7;19vp,42,5;1hke,71,4;1uxc,78,4;1ozy,103,4;19r7,119,3	e:29qk,23,5~29qk,23,5
