1x1k|n|A root. ; A kind of guitar, the notes of which were produced by a small wheel or wheel-like arrangement; an instrument similar to the hurdy-gurdy. ; The noise produced by the surf of the sea dashing upon the shore. See Rut. ; A frequent repetition of forms of speech without attention to the meaning; mere repetition; as, to learn rules by rote.	V:19at,54,16~19at,54,16	n:293l,43,8;851,36,1;97,4,3~293l,43,8;97,4,3;851,36,1	N:1cyh,110,4;19at,34,4;1pyl,30,1~1cyh,110,4;19at,34,4;1pyl,30,1
1x1k|v|To learn or repeat by rote. ; To go out by rotation or succession; to rotate.	o:1cyh,116,6;1cyb,114,1~1cyh,116,6;1cyb,114,1
